We are inside method toArray() returning Object[].

We need to assert that the length of the returned array is one greater than the collection size. The method returns `Arrays.copyOf(elementData, size);` Actually copyOf copies elementData of length size, so resulting array length equals size. But comment says length is one greater than collection size. That's maybe bug. Anyway we need to produce assertion reflecting comment.

We need to refer to return value: \result. The collection size is this.size()? There's method size() that returns number of elements. Use this.size().

Thus assert: assert \result.length == this.size() + 1;

But need to use Java syntax? In JML style, we use .length field. So: assert \result.length == this.size() + 1;

Make sure to use correct syntax: \result is an Object[]. So .length is fine.

Thus final answer:

<code>assert \result.length == this.size() + 1;</code>

